From 40440c33a7869a2c67aa509626f5abce82919356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:33:45 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/33] mdadm: do not ask about a bitmap when creating a
 container

mdadm --create of a container of external metadata gives no level, so
s.level is UnSet (0xfffe), and the check for the question about a
write-intent bitmap, s.level >= 1, lets it through.  Answering yes
then fails the create: "bitmaps not meaningful with level container".

Ask only when a level is given.  Without one, the array is a container,
which has no bitmap, or Create() refuses it for the missing level.

IMSM container of two loop devices, "y" on stdin: before, the create
fails as above; with the change it is created and nothing is asked.  A
RAID1 still gets the question.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.

Fixes: e97c4e18c847 ("mdadm: ask user if bitmap is not set")
---
 mdadm.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mdadm.c b/mdadm.c
index 64fbc101..3332bbad 100644
--- a/mdadm.c
+++ b/mdadm.c
@@ -1582,8 +1582,12 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 			break;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * No level: a container of external metadata, which has no
+		 * bitmap (or an error further on), so no question about one.
+		 */
 		if (s.btype == BitmapUnknown) {
-			if (c.runstop != 1 && s.level >= 1 &&
+			if (c.runstop != 1 && s.level >= 1 && s.level != UnSet &&
 			    ask("To optimize recovery speed, it is recommended to enable write-intent bitmap, do you want to enable it now?"))
 				s.btype = BitmapInternal;
 			else
